		"nodes": {
			"11": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": true
					},
					"font-size": {
						"type": "float",
						"value": 19
					},
					"text": {
						"type": "string",
						"value": "READ\n\nRead will output the value at the given index. \nIf you have a collection running from 1 to 10 and you read out index 5 you will get a 6 (remember that collections start at index 0). \nThe node can be set the index to wrap or clamp depending on your needs\n\n It is also possible to feed the Read node an collection for its index inlet. \nThis way you can read out multiple values (the Sequence node is a good candidate to go into the index inlet).\nBut the Span node is better at this most of the time.\n\nRead can also interpolate between two indices.\nCheck out the examples to see that in action."
					}
				},
				"bounds": {
					"height": 285.09722900390625,
					"width": 708.33697509765625,
					"x": 425.097412109375,
					"y": 29.08879470825195312
				},
				"class": {
					"id": "77697265-3C1D-467D-A722-0FC566538374",
					"version": 1
				},
				"clock": "video",
				"color": "ffd0c117",
				"constants": {},
				"hidden": [
					"text",
					"alignment",
					"font-size",
					"fill"
				],
				"name": "Comment",
				"thumbnail_visible": true
			},
			"62": {
				"attributes": {
					"alignment": {
						"type": "integer",
						"value": 0
					},
					"fill": {
						"type": "bool",
						"value": false
